														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1970047">
									

<p>My main criticism of this is that apparently no research is being done on these subjects. Nothing is known about this thing, and apparently no one is even trying to find out. What happens if someone who already has early Alzheimer's comes in contact with 1693-1? Why don't we just cut out their vocal cords so they are no longer infectious? Or use speech-to-text software to find out what the infected are saying in a safe manner? Why haven't we been examining their brains once they die? Alzheimer's is very easy to confirm post-mortem, and the whole charade would be broken after one or two D-class were found to be fakes in autopsy.</p>
<p>I like the idea that the d-class are pulling a fast one on the Foundation, but i just can't see how this would possibly trick them.</p>

